WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.230
It is short and fast.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.960
Most scholars think it
is the earliest Gospel,

3
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.640
written about 65 to 75 CE.

4
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.090
Its writer never gives his name.

5
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:16.030
An early bishop, Papias, said Mark
wrote down what Peter remembered.

6
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.950
And its oldest copies end
at chapter 16, verse 8.

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.510
The verses after that were added later.

8
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.250
So why should a book this old
still guide anyone's life today?

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.380
In this mission, you'll find
out who probably wrote Mark,

10
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.900
and for whom.

11
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.350
Then you'll weigh up whether its
miracle stories really happened,

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.520
and why people disagree.

13
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:42.270
Your mission: find out why this
old book still guides lives today,

14
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.390
and for whom.
